WEBVTT

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.227
[dragons snuffling]

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.861
[Drago grunts]

00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:29.202
[Snotlout] Could this day get any worse?

00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:30.161
[Tuffnut] Let me see.

00:00:30.245 --> 00:00:33.123
We're gonna jump into freezing cold
water, then die from drowning.

00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:34.416
[Eret] Looks refreshing.

00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:36.710
Please, ladies first.

00:00:37.919 --> 00:00:40.797
You are a steaming heap of dragon…

00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:42.549
-Duck.
-[men grunt]

00:00:45.802 --> 00:00:46.803
Warn the others!

00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:48.471
Get them, you son of an Eret.

00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:50.599
[men grunting]

00:00:50.682 --> 00:00:51.683
[Tuffnut] Take that!

00:00:56.104 --> 00:00:57.606
[man groaning]

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.150
Okay, I love you again.

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:03.320
-[exhales]
-Pathetic. You can still jump.

00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:06.364
So, are we going to save your
dragons and get out of here, or not?

00:01:06.448 --> 00:01:07.490
Hmm.

00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:10.535
[Eret] Check every trap.
They're here somewhere.

00:01:15.999 --> 00:01:18.043
[grunting]

00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:21.212
Meatlug?

00:01:21.296 --> 00:01:22.297
[groans]

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.215
[straining] Anyone coming?

00:01:24.382 --> 00:01:27.010
I don't know.
You just keep doing what you are doing.

00:01:27.093 --> 00:01:28.928
Keep cranking.

00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:34.351
[grunts]

00:01:45.695 --> 00:01:48.657
Thank you for saving my life.

00:01:50.241 --> 00:01:51.368
[gurgles]

00:01:52.911 --> 00:01:54.704
Now let me return the favor.

00:01:55.538 --> 00:01:58.083
Mom, you'd never even recognize it.

00:01:58.249 --> 00:02:02.087
Where we used to make weapons,
we now build saddles, wing-slings.

00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:04.422
We even fix dragon teeth!

00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:06.633
You wouldn't believe
how much everything's changed.

00:02:06.841 --> 00:02:09.427
Your son has changed Berk for the better.

00:02:09.552 --> 00:02:11.221
I think we did well with this one, Val.

00:02:11.388 --> 00:02:12.514
-Thanks, Dad.
-Oh!

00:02:13.682 --> 00:02:15.558
[Stoick chuckles] Oh, I got it. I got it.

00:02:15.642 --> 00:02:17.310
[whimpers]

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.690
[retching]

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:30.573
I'm a little out of practice.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.534
Well, you know…

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:35.370
-I didn't marry you for your cooking.
-[Gobber] I hope not.

00:02:35.537 --> 00:02:39.082
Her meatballs could
kill more beasts than a battle-axe.

00:02:39.207 --> 00:02:41.918
I've still got a few
knocking around in here. [laughs]

00:02:42.085 --> 00:02:44.629
And once you move back in,
with all your dragons…

00:02:44.796 --> 00:02:46.923
Drago won't even stand a chance.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.883
Everything will be okay!

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.721
Slow down, son. It's a lot to take in.

00:02:53.221 --> 00:02:54.931
[Hiccup] Oh, gotcha.

00:02:58.893 --> 00:03:00.520
[Stoick whistling]

00:03:02.522 --> 00:03:04.983
Oh, I love this one.

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.949
[continues whistling]

00:03:20.749 --> 00:03:22.876
Remember our song, Val?

00:03:24.294 --> 00:03:30.467
♪ I'll swim and sail on savage seas ♪

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.514
♪ With ne'er a fear of drowning ♪

00:03:38.266 --> 00:03:43.271
♪ And gladly ride the waves of life ♪

00:03:44.773 --> 00:03:49.110
♪ If you will marry me ♪

00:03:51.613 --> 00:03:54.157
♪ No scorching sun ♪

00:03:54.324 --> 00:03:57.952
♪ Nor freezing cold will stop… ♪

00:03:58.119 --> 00:04:01.498
♪ Will stop me on my journey ♪

00:04:01.623 --> 00:04:03.374
Sorry. [chuckles]

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.168
[exhales]

00:04:06.002 --> 00:04:11.591
♪ If you will promise me your heart ♪

00:04:15.929 --> 00:04:17.764
♪ And love… ♪

00:04:19.891 --> 00:04:21.309
[sighs]

00:04:23.311 --> 00:04:29.734
♪ And love me for eternity ♪

00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:33.279
♪ My dearest one ♪

00:04:33.488 --> 00:04:35.490
♪ My darling dear ♪

00:04:35.657 --> 00:04:39.661
♪ Your mighty words astound me ♪

00:04:39.828 --> 00:04:42.997
♪ But I've no need of mighty deeds ♪

00:04:43.164 --> 00:04:46.376
♪ When I feel your arms around me ♪

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:48.878
♪ But I would bring you rings of gold ♪

00:04:49.003 --> 00:04:50.755
♪ I'd even sing you poetry ♪

00:04:50.839 --> 00:04:51.840
Whoo! Oh, would you?

00:04:51.923 --> 00:04:54.092
♪ And I would keep you from all harm ♪

00:04:54.259 --> 00:04:56.928
♪ If you would stay beside me ♪

00:04:57.095 --> 00:04:58.888
♪ I have no use for rings of gold ♪

00:04:58.972 --> 00:05:01.266
♪ I care not for your poetry ♪

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:03.518
♪ I only want your hand to hold ♪

00:05:03.685 --> 00:05:05.186
♪ I only want you near me ♪

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:07.856
[Stoick and Valka]
♪ To love and kiss, to sweetly hold ♪

00:05:07.939 --> 00:05:09.899
♪ For the dancing and the dreaming ♪

00:05:10.108 --> 00:05:12.110
♪ Through all life's
sorrows and delights ♪

00:05:12.193 --> 00:05:13.862
♪ I'll keep your love inside me ♪

00:05:13.945 --> 00:05:15.738
♪ I will swim and sail on savage seas ♪

00:05:15.822 --> 00:05:17.532
♪ With ne'er a fear of drowning ♪

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:19.617
♪ And gladly ride the waves of life ♪

00:05:19.784 --> 00:05:21.786
♪ If you will marry me ♪

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.705
-[both laughing]
-[Gobber vocalizing]

00:05:24.789 --> 00:05:25.790
♪ I'm still going ♪

00:05:25.874 --> 00:05:27.041
-Gobber!
-I'm done.

00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:29.544
-[sighs]
-[laughs]

00:05:30.253 --> 00:05:33.047
I thought I would have to die
before we could have that dance again.

00:05:33.214 --> 00:05:35.717
No need for drastic measures.

00:05:36.384 --> 00:05:38.428
For you, my dear…

00:05:39.179 --> 00:05:40.722
Anything.

00:05:41.681 --> 00:05:43.683
Will you come home, Val?

00:05:45.185 --> 00:05:47.687
Will you be my wife once again?

00:05:50.148 --> 00:05:51.524
[gasps]

00:05:51.608 --> 00:05:53.067
[both laugh]

00:05:54.235 --> 00:05:56.905
We can be a family! What do you say?

00:05:57.071 --> 00:05:58.573
Oh…

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:01.951
Yes.

00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:06.539
Great! I'll do the cooking.

00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:11.252
Thank Odin you didn't listen to me, son.

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:12.921
We never would have found each other.

00:06:13.004 --> 00:06:14.589
[dragons shrieking]

00:06:15.131 --> 00:06:16.674
Toothless?

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:21.638
What's happening?

